.Dd October 4, 2026
.Dt COMPACTION 7
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm compaction
.Nd context compaction as the OOM killer of the language model stack
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Em Compaction \&Is the \&New \&OOM
.Pp
Context compaction as the OOM killer of the language model stack.
.Pp
Canonical copy:
.Bl -item -compact -offset indent
.It
.Lk https://coetzeestefan.substack.com/p/compaction-is-the-new-oom
.El
.Sh TERMS
Definitions in the wording of the published piece.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Compaction
The harness summarising a full context window and discarding the original
history so the session can continue.
.It \&OOM killer
The part of the Linux kernel that picks and kills a process when RAM and
swap are both exhausted.
.It Registers
Here, the context window; the only memory the model works on directly.
.It Swap, paging out
Moving state from the context window to a durable tier (tracker, vault,
instruction file) during the work, so that losing the window loses nothing
that matters.
.It Error-and-fix pair
A failed attempt together with what worked instead; the unit of knowledge a
session builds up and a summary tends to drop.
.It Hibernation file
The session handover; the state written to durable storage before a session
ends, read by the next one at start.
.It \&Wet, cured, re-wetted
A session at cold start, a session that holds its line after running for a
while, and a session after compaction.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr instruction-file 5 ,
.Xr golem 7 ,
